<header><p class="st-kicker">other · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Dominion of Pakistan</h1><p class="st-meta">1947 CE – 1956 CE · capital Karachi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Pakistan's first form as an independent state, a dominion of the British Commonwealth in two wings separated by a thousand miles of India.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The demand for a separate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> for Muslims, adopted by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/all-india-muslim-league">All-India Muslim League</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore-resolution">Lahore Resolution</a> of 1940, led to the partition of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/british-raj">British Raj</a>. On 14 August 1947 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominion</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-republic-of-pakistan">Pakistan</a> came into being, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ali-jinnah">Muhammad Ali Jinnah</a> as Governor-General and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karachi">Karachi</a> as capital, comprising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-pakistan">West Pakistan</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bangladesh">East Bengal</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The new state faced the upheaval of partition, with millions of refugees and massacres, and war with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dominion-of-india">Dominion of India</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> in 1947 to 1948. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ali-jinnah">Jinnah</a> died in 1948 and prime minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaquat-ali-khan">Liaquat Ali Khan</a> was assassinated in 1951. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/objectives-resolution">Objectives Resolution</a> of 1949 set Islamic principles for a constitution, while the Bengali Language Movement of 1952 exposed tensions between the two wings.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After years of constitutional deadlock and the dismissal of the Constituent Assembly in 1954, a constitution was adopted on 23 March 1956, declaring the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-republic-of-pakistan">Islamic Republic of Pakistan</a> and ending dominion status.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/dominion-of-pakistan.jpg" alt="Dominion of Pakistan" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: User:Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Pakistan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1947 CE – 1956 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Karachi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Muhammad Ali Jinnah, Liaquat Ali Khan, Ghulam Muhammad</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Urdu, Bengali, English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, <a href="/countries/bangladesh">Bangladesh</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pakistan (dominion)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1952&amp;focus=dominion-of-pakistan" aria-label="Dominion of Pakistan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6458 1263 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Dominion of Pakistan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6778 1519L7364 1602M6778 1519L6864 1211M6778 1519L6738 1372M6778 1519L6738 1372M6778 1519L6867 1359M6778 1519L6806 1424M6778 1519L6811 1139M6778 1519L6836 1176M6778 1519L6820 1161M6778 1519L6853 1189M6778 1519L6858 1190M6778 1519L6879 1123M6778 1519L6866 1154M6778 1519L6751 1470M6778 1519L6710 1388M6778 1519L6666 1478"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1602h0M6864 1211h0M6738 1372h0M6738 1372h0M6867 1359h0M6806 1424h0M6811 1139h0M6836 1176h0M6820 1161h0M6853 1189h0M6858 1190h0M6879 1123h0M6866 1154h0M6751 1470h0M6710 1388h0M6666 1478h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6778 1519h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6778 1519h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Karachi. <a href="/atlas?year=1